WEBVTT

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:16.700
Here. Are we good now?

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:18.830
Thank you very much!

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:24.040
Th-Thank goodness! Now Marika's
finally an official employee.

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:27.950
Now let's explore that weird mechanized dungeon!

00:00:27.950 --> 00:00:29.750
Yup! Let's do this!

00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:33.910
We'll get the rare-earth and
obtain the old man's legacy!

00:00:33.910 --> 00:00:38.290
The thing is, even Rivar
got hurt in that dungeon.

00:00:38.290 --> 00:00:40.910
Hmph! Buzz off!

00:00:40.910 --> 00:00:44.500
There's dangerous maju in there,
so let's watch out.

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:49.040
Although I'll be holding the fort,
I'll pray for your success!

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:53.040
Let's go out there and show 'em
we mean business, guys!

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:55.910
Is everyone ready? Cheer with me!

00:00:55.910 --> 00:00:59.500
Kibou, fight!

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:01.410
Yeah!

00:01:02.410 --> 00:01:04.790
You do this every time?

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:07.000
No... This is a first.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.370
I just went with the flow, but...

00:01:09.370 --> 00:01:11.700
That was so embarrassing.

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:13.750
S-Sorry.

00:01:18.870 --> 00:01:21.660
<i>Let's dive right into today's letters</i>

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:27.160
<i>It's "Personal Advice" and the title is</i>

00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:29.160
<i>"Hurry into Love! Hurry Love! Love!!"</i>

00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:43.750
<i>Hey, hear me out.</i>
<i>There's something I really wanna say</i>

00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:48.950
<i>You've got courage to follow</i>
<i>your dreams which is why I chose you</i>

00:01:48.950 --> 00:01:51.080
<i>Is it a risky bet</i>

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:56.580
<i>Despite no experience,</i>
<i>we jumped right in together</i>

00:01:56.580 --> 00:02:00.040
<i>And this unpredictable story</i>

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:06.120
<i>Is your creation--</i>
<i>a heart-throbbing innovation</i>

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:08.580
<i>Quickly! Quickly! Take me along</i>

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:11.200
<i>On a bittersweet love venture</i>

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:16.000
<i>Ah! Measured not by skill</i>
<i>but by scale and romance</i>

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:21.040
<i>Hurry! Hurry! Boldly, subtly, show your appeal</i>

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:26.080
<i>Ah! Our meeting was a miracle</i>
<i>that can't be neglected</i>

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:29.660
<i>It's galactic level</i>

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:33.160
<i>I see. Sounds like you're head over heels.</i>

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:38.500
<i>Let's tell him, just like battle</i>

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:40.870
<i>"Hurry into Love! Hurry Love! Love!!"</i>

00:02:40.870 --> 00:02:43.250
<i>Everyone, Hurry! Hurry Love! Love!!</i>

00:02:44.830 --> 00:02:50.830
"Episode Six: Business Goals"

00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:54.160
You're kidding! What is this?

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:57.580
So this is the mechanized dungeon?

00:02:58.910 --> 00:03:03.370
This feels like metal,
but almost like it's alive...

00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:06.790
Careful. I wouldn't touch that if I were you.

00:03:06.790 --> 00:03:11.660
She's right, Makoto. What if you
get corrupted or something?

00:03:11.660 --> 00:03:15.700
I think the anomaly comes
from within. Let's keep moving.

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:19.910
Right. Let's get the rare-earth,
whatever it takes!

00:03:19.910 --> 00:03:25.540
This is probably a "bug." It might
be related to my dad's disappearance.

00:03:25.540 --> 00:03:27.160
Come on, President!

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:29.750
Huh? R-Right!

00:03:36.660 --> 00:03:38.450
Subaru, let's go in.

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:43.080
If we don't hurry, other companies
will get the jump on us.

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:44.750
I think I'll pass.

00:03:44.750 --> 00:03:47.000
--Huh?
--Wh-Why?

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:49.950
If Imperial gets bested
by some other company,

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:52.750
people will lose confidence in us.

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:57.200
This dungeon has too many dangerous unknowns.

00:03:57.200 --> 00:04:03.160
If our exploration ends in failure,
it will damage our reputation.

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:07.500
Perhaps, but we've heard
reports of rare-earth inside.

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:11.500
Luckily, we've already reached
our quota this quarter.

00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:16.250
There's no need to take
the risk for additional profit.

00:04:16.250 --> 00:04:23.290
B-But start-ups and cottage companies
like Cyedge and Kibou have gone in.

00:04:23.290 --> 00:04:27.660
And we'll learn if taking the plunge
first pays off for them.

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:30.830
This will let us see what they're made of.

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:40.080
It's like the deeper we go, the worse it gets.

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:45.700
Yeah. But it's strangely quiet.
And there're no maju either.

00:04:45.700 --> 00:04:48.700
It's like the calm before the storm.

00:04:48.700 --> 00:04:51.620
Let's just hope it stays that way.

00:04:51.620 --> 00:04:56.250
Keep an eye out for anything strange.
If you see something, let us--

00:04:57.370 --> 00:04:58.910
Uh!

00:04:58.910 --> 00:05:01.200
President! Was that...?!

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:04.000
Yeah! I've got a bad feeling!

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:09.500
Y-You're kidding!

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:11.620
That's so cliche!

00:05:12.830 --> 00:05:15.120
E-Everyone, run!

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:16.910
What?! Uh, wait up!

00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:19.910
Rivar failed to mention this!

00:05:19.910 --> 00:05:23.160
I-It might've changed since he came through!

00:05:23.160 --> 00:05:26.200
D-Does that even matter right now?!

00:05:28.370 --> 00:05:29.830
Another trap?!

00:05:29.830 --> 00:05:31.950
This always happens in films!

00:05:31.950 --> 00:05:33.410
Hurry up! Jump!

00:05:33.410 --> 00:05:36.330
I-I'm not even close to athletic!

00:05:36.330 --> 00:05:41.160
Just do it! You can't research
maju and plants if you're dead!

00:05:41.160 --> 00:05:42.410
Here goes!

00:05:45.410 --> 00:05:47.200
Oh, shoot!

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:52.040
I-I'm falling!

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:55.450
President! You okay?!

00:05:57.160 --> 00:06:00.200
Th-This place is the pits.

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:06.500
W-We somehow survived.

00:06:06.500 --> 00:06:10.660
We were so close to being crushed
or smushed like pancakes.

00:06:10.660 --> 00:06:15.580
While I do love flower pressing,
I'd rather not be flattened myself.

00:06:15.580 --> 00:06:18.000
Can you guys drop it already?

00:06:22.200 --> 00:06:23.830
M-More traps?

00:06:23.830 --> 00:06:26.950
If this gets any more cliche, I'll be impressed!

00:06:29.160 --> 00:06:32.370
I-It's hopeless! We're about to be crushed!

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:39.040
Ow, ow, ow!

00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:42.870
Th-That was another close call.

00:06:42.870 --> 00:06:45.830
Yeah. But, look...

00:06:45.830 --> 00:06:47.870
Huh?

00:06:47.870 --> 00:06:49.330
This is...!

00:06:54.410 --> 00:06:56.660
Mama!

00:06:58.870 --> 00:07:00.750
Shit, not again.

00:07:00.750 --> 00:07:03.870
Could you please stop yelling like that?

00:07:03.870 --> 00:07:07.080
Keep it up and I'll send you to the hospital.

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:12.500
Hmph. This place is an employee perk.
I'll milk it for all it's worth.

00:07:12.500 --> 00:07:16.000
Well, you're fully entitled to do so.

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:18.910
Did you have a nightmare or something?

00:07:18.910 --> 00:07:24.540
I can't stop hearing the voices
of those damn maju!

00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:29.290
Is this as deep as it goes?

00:07:29.290 --> 00:07:31.830
It's all so cold and lifeless.

00:07:31.830 --> 00:07:33.870
Let's get the goods and scram.

00:07:33.870 --> 00:07:36.700
That's what a thief would say.

00:07:36.700 --> 00:07:38.750
It feels like a factory.

00:07:38.750 --> 00:07:42.750
Yeah. Do you think the
anomaly spreads from here?

00:07:42.750 --> 00:07:48.250
Hmm, I wonder. It might
be caused by something else.

00:07:51.290 --> 00:07:53.160
Th-That was Akari!

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:55.000
O-Oh, no!

00:07:56.790 --> 00:07:58.700
N-No way!

00:08:00.330 --> 00:08:02.250
Guys, you okay?!

00:08:02.250 --> 00:08:04.910
You're not gonna believe it! Look!

00:08:04.910 --> 00:08:06.700
Huh? Wha...?!

00:08:09.450 --> 00:08:12.540
Rare-earth! And tons of it!

00:08:12.540 --> 00:08:16.870
W-We can totally pay off
the inheritance tax with this!

00:08:18.040 --> 00:08:20.580
My dad's legacy is ours!

00:08:22.700 --> 00:08:24.370
President! Maju!

00:08:24.370 --> 00:08:25.870
There they are!

00:08:25.870 --> 00:08:28.950
Wait, huh?! What are these guys?!

00:08:32.500 --> 00:08:34.540
Their bodies are mechanized!

00:08:34.540 --> 00:08:36.950
I've never seen maju like this!

00:08:36.950 --> 00:08:38.660
Careful! Here they come!

00:08:53.040 --> 00:08:55.910
Hmph. That was a piece of cake.

00:08:55.910 --> 00:09:00.620
That's a shame. I was hoping
to learn more about 'em.

00:09:00.620 --> 00:09:04.910
Before you go researching maju,
let's grab all this rare-earth.

00:09:04.910 --> 00:09:10.250
Wait. Rivar was seriously injured here.
There's gotta be more to this.

00:09:13.700 --> 00:09:15.540
What, there's another?

00:09:15.540 --> 00:09:17.540
Looks kinda scrawny to me.

00:09:17.540 --> 00:09:21.700
True, but it seems different from the others.

00:09:28.540 --> 00:09:29.870
Huh? No way!

00:09:29.870 --> 00:09:32.080
What the heck is going on?!

00:09:32.080 --> 00:09:35.370
I-It sounds like they're saying something!

00:09:35.370 --> 00:09:40.910
--Overtime... Overtime... Overtime...
--Work on weekends...

00:09:40.910 --> 00:09:45.830
--Restructuring... Restructuring...
--It's worth it... It's worth it...

00:09:45.830 --> 00:09:48.200
S-Such vile thoughts!

00:09:48.200 --> 00:09:50.750
We'll just have to beat 'em again!

00:09:50.750 --> 00:09:52.410
Leave it to me!

00:09:54.580 --> 00:09:58.580
H-Hey! Stay away from me!

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:06.290
A-Again?!

00:10:06.290 --> 00:10:08.200
What's with these guys?!

00:10:08.200 --> 00:10:11.370
Their eyes are freaking me out!

00:10:11.370 --> 00:10:13.500
We'll beat 'em as much as it takes!

00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:16.000
Wait! If you get too close...!

00:10:20.370 --> 00:10:21.450
You okay?!

00:10:21.450 --> 00:10:22.830
Y-Yeah.

00:10:22.830 --> 00:10:24.870
It was only a scratch.

00:10:24.870 --> 00:10:27.000
Th-Thank goodness.

00:10:27.000 --> 00:10:28.290
H-Huh?!

00:10:28.290 --> 00:10:30.410
Wh-What's happening?

00:10:30.410 --> 00:10:33.370
My body's moving on its own!

00:10:35.410 --> 00:10:38.250
Overtime... Overtime...

00:10:38.250 --> 00:10:42.040
Work on weekends... Work on weekends...

00:10:42.040 --> 00:10:45.120
N-No! It can't be...!

00:10:49.250 --> 00:10:51.620
Restructuring... Restructuring...

00:10:51.620 --> 00:10:54.040
It's worth it...

00:10:54.040 --> 00:10:57.250
Wh-What's going on, President?!

00:10:57.250 --> 00:11:00.580
If you're hit, you become a corporate slave!

00:11:00.580 --> 00:11:06.290
"Corporate Slave"
Corporate slave?! That's an
affliction even worse than death!

00:11:06.290 --> 00:11:11.620
"Gloom"
Yeah. It's where you keep working
till your body gives up.

00:11:11.620 --> 00:11:14.580
"Gloom"
D-Dear me!

00:11:14.580 --> 00:11:20.370
The boss is using its power
to keep reviving corporate slaves!

00:11:20.370 --> 00:11:24.700
That must be the boss! The boss maju!

00:11:24.700 --> 00:11:29.540
What now, President?!
At this rate, my poor sister...!

00:11:29.540 --> 00:11:33.160
Corporate slavery is usually caused by bosses.

00:11:33.160 --> 00:11:36.500
Once they're out of the picture,
people get better.

00:11:36.500 --> 00:11:39.410
Then let's defeat the boss maju!

00:11:39.410 --> 00:11:42.290
--The thing is, Akari and Marika
are our heavy hitters!

00:11:42.290 --> 00:11:45.580
--Overtime... Overtime...
--Work on weekends...
--The thing is, Akari and Marika
are our heavy hitters!

00:11:48.040 --> 00:11:48.950
I'll do it.

00:11:48.950 --> 00:11:52.120
--Huh?
--Y-You can't! That's crazy!

00:11:53.120 --> 00:11:56.870
The boss maju can't be very strong by itself.

00:11:56.870 --> 00:12:00.040
I'll slip through the other maju and attack.

00:12:00.040 --> 00:12:03.200
But Makoto needs to use healing magic on them.

00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:05.080
Healing magic?

00:12:05.080 --> 00:12:09.040
If I do that, the maju will get stronger!

00:12:09.040 --> 00:12:12.290
It's okay! Just trust me!

00:12:12.290 --> 00:12:14.160
Mmm. All right.

00:12:14.160 --> 00:12:15.450
Thanks!

00:12:15.450 --> 00:12:18.830
Once Yutoria distracts
the subordinates from afar,

00:12:18.830 --> 00:12:21.040
I want Makoto to heal them!

00:12:21.040 --> 00:12:22.040
You've got it!

00:12:22.040 --> 00:12:23.790
I'll try!

00:12:23.790 --> 00:12:25.830
Okay! Let's go!

00:12:28.040 --> 00:12:29.370
Now!

00:12:29.370 --> 00:12:31.250
Hey, you!

00:12:31.250 --> 00:12:36.120
If you keep slaving away like that,
you'll just wear yourself out!

00:12:37.750 --> 00:12:40.200
Rate Heal!

00:12:43.450 --> 00:12:46.080
Huh? They stopped moving!

00:12:47.700 --> 00:12:49.700
Yes! Just like I thought!

00:12:49.700 --> 00:12:52.410
Wh-What do you mean, President?!

00:12:52.410 --> 00:12:58.790
They're so used to being abused,
they don't understand heals or support!

00:12:58.790 --> 00:13:02.790
Being in a healthy workplace
confuses them so much,

00:13:02.790 --> 00:13:05.410
they're actually taking time off!

00:13:05.410 --> 00:13:11.370
Now I can attack the source of this
toxic work environment, the boss!

00:13:11.370 --> 00:13:12.700
The boss...?

00:13:14.870 --> 00:13:18.000
Ack! It's my fault for acting so smug!

00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:20.790
P-President!

00:13:24.910 --> 00:13:26.080
Huh?

00:13:29.450 --> 00:13:31.160
Y-Yutoria!

00:13:31.160 --> 00:13:35.540
You always get carried away
when explaining things, President.

00:13:35.540 --> 00:13:37.870
I-I'll be more careful.

00:13:37.870 --> 00:13:39.830
But, thank goodness!

00:13:39.830 --> 00:13:43.750
Now that the boss is gone,
there's no more forced labor!

00:13:47.660 --> 00:13:50.080
I-It's finally over!

00:13:50.080 --> 00:13:52.000
I can rest at last!

00:13:52.000 --> 00:13:54.950
That wiped me out, too!

00:14:00.120 --> 00:14:02.250
That's the last of it.

00:14:02.250 --> 00:14:06.790
We're so lucky we found
that shortcut. With this, at last...!

00:14:06.790 --> 00:14:09.790
Yes! The inheritance will be ours!

00:14:09.790 --> 00:14:14.700
And I know that's great and all,
but that seriously was the worst!

00:14:14.700 --> 00:14:18.660
Being forced to work like that...
Having to say weird things...

00:14:18.660 --> 00:14:21.250
Being a corporate slave sucks.

00:14:21.250 --> 00:14:26.660
When I grow up and become an adult,
is that what work will be like?

00:14:26.660 --> 00:14:29.910
I-It's not like that for everyone.

00:14:29.910 --> 00:14:32.250
It hurts to hear!

00:14:32.250 --> 00:14:35.620
Anyway! Since I had to go
through hell to get this,

00:14:35.620 --> 00:14:38.750
let's get our money and race to the museum!

00:14:38.750 --> 00:14:40.540
Right!

00:14:40.540 --> 00:14:44.290
It kinda hurts to spend all of it though.

00:14:47.660 --> 00:14:52.120
Thank you. The inheritance tax
has been paid in full now.

00:14:52.120 --> 00:14:54.040
This is your receipt.

00:14:54.040 --> 00:14:56.540
Does this mean...?

00:14:56.540 --> 00:15:02.330
Like I mentioned before, now you're
welcome to claim the entire legacy.

00:15:02.330 --> 00:15:05.200
Please help yourself to it.

00:15:05.200 --> 00:15:07.080
Thank you!

00:15:08.120 --> 00:15:09.580
Look at this!

00:15:09.580 --> 00:15:11.330
The old man's legacy!

00:15:11.330 --> 00:15:15.950
Awesome! This sword cuts, like,
three times better than mine!

00:15:15.950 --> 00:15:18.330
This staff looks incredible!

00:15:18.330 --> 00:15:22.200
And there's even grimoires
like this! Pretty cool!

00:15:22.200 --> 00:15:25.700
This will help us out so much financially!

00:15:25.700 --> 00:15:27.370
We did it, President!

00:15:27.370 --> 00:15:30.160
No more equipment worries for us!

00:15:30.160 --> 00:15:33.330
Yup! We can finally relax a bit!

00:15:33.330 --> 00:15:35.290
But...

00:15:35.290 --> 00:15:39.500
I wonder why my dad donated such good stuff?

00:15:39.500 --> 00:15:45.290
That's a good point. Some of this
stuff seems more like treasure.

00:15:46.500 --> 00:15:48.450
Huh?

00:15:48.450 --> 00:15:50.160
Why is this here?

00:15:50.160 --> 00:15:52.540
Is that a projector?

00:15:52.540 --> 00:15:59.160
It looks similar to the device for
"The Dungeon Clearing Pictorial Tutorial."

00:16:02.540 --> 00:16:04.500
D-Dad?!

00:16:04.500 --> 00:16:07.290
What is this?!

00:16:10.500 --> 00:16:16.040
Yo! Long time no see, Minato.
Yutoria. Guide. Akari. Makoto.

00:16:16.040 --> 00:16:19.910
I bet you've got some new employees, too.

00:16:19.910 --> 00:16:22.790
So you've managed to claim my legacy?

00:16:22.790 --> 00:16:28.410
You won't be happy to hear it, but I went
out of my way to donate this stuff.

00:16:28.410 --> 00:16:30.290
Huh? What's he mean?

00:16:30.290 --> 00:16:33.290
I see. So that's how it is!

00:16:33.290 --> 00:16:35.870
Figured it out, huh?

00:16:35.870 --> 00:16:39.410
That's right. It was to test you guys.

00:16:39.410 --> 00:16:44.500
If you couldn't pay off the inheritance tax,
you couldn't run the company.

00:16:44.500 --> 00:16:47.250
The legacy was a test for us.

00:16:47.250 --> 00:16:51.910
It was quite the challenge,
but we passed it in the end.

00:16:51.910 --> 00:16:56.330
Now then, let's move on to the real deal.

00:16:56.330 --> 00:17:01.870
By the time you're seeing this,
I'm already inside the Big Gate.

00:17:01.870 --> 00:17:05.870
The Big Gate... He really did go in...

00:17:09.750 --> 00:17:14.250
Truth is, something strange
is happening with the Big Gate.

00:17:14.250 --> 00:17:20.540
And I don't know what, but I'm
pretty sure it's not gonna end well.

00:17:20.540 --> 00:17:24.660
If this keeps up, all of
Gatepia will be in trouble.

00:17:24.660 --> 00:17:28.950
Anomalies will start popping up all over.

00:17:28.950 --> 00:17:32.700
I'm gonna figure out the
reason and make it stop.

00:17:32.700 --> 00:17:36.660
Then, the Big Gate is why
the dungeon was like that.

00:17:36.660 --> 00:17:41.750
It's a dangerous mission and
I might not make it out in one piece.

00:17:41.750 --> 00:17:45.410
But I promise you, I will finish the job.

00:17:45.410 --> 00:17:46.660
Which is why...

00:17:47.950 --> 00:17:50.290
Come and join me.

00:17:50.290 --> 00:17:51.790
Dad...

00:17:51.790 --> 00:17:54.200
But I don't mean right away.

00:17:54.200 --> 00:17:59.660
Once the company's on the right track,
come find me and lend me a hand.

00:18:03.290 --> 00:18:06.200
I'll be waiting for you guys.

00:18:08.200 --> 00:18:10.870
My dad's in the Big Gate...

00:18:10.870 --> 00:18:15.080
What's more, he's waiting
for us to come after him.

00:18:15.080 --> 00:18:17.620
I wonder what he's thinking?

00:18:17.620 --> 00:18:19.660
Maybe there's some other clue.

00:18:23.120 --> 00:18:24.620
Huh?

00:18:24.620 --> 00:18:26.370
Look at this!

00:18:27.750 --> 00:18:31.910
That's a group picture we took a few years back.

00:18:31.910 --> 00:18:35.370
It's from before Minato became president.

00:18:35.370 --> 00:18:37.790
That brings back memories!

00:18:37.790 --> 00:18:42.040
Wasn't it his idea to get
a picture with everyone in it?

00:18:42.040 --> 00:18:44.160
Yeah, I remember that.

00:18:44.160 --> 00:18:49.370
He was never one to take pictures,
so I thought it strange.

00:18:51.200 --> 00:18:56.540
But why did he leave the
picture with this other stuff?

00:18:56.540 --> 00:19:01.410
Because his employees must
have been precious to him.

00:19:01.410 --> 00:19:03.660
Huh? You mean us?

00:19:03.660 --> 00:19:09.120
Yup. I'm sure this picture is one
of my dad's greatest treasures.

00:19:09.120 --> 00:19:14.700
He always said that his
employees were like his family.

00:19:14.700 --> 00:19:16.500
Family...

00:19:23.000 --> 00:19:26.370
Well, he never would've said that to our faces.

00:19:26.370 --> 00:19:28.620
That's so like him, isn't it?

00:19:28.620 --> 00:19:31.950
Yeah. He was just that kind of person.

00:19:31.950 --> 00:19:36.910
I don't know much about the old man,
but he sounds pretty cool.

00:19:38.000 --> 00:19:40.750
Wait... There's something else in here, too!

00:19:40.750 --> 00:19:41.910
Huh?!

00:19:41.910 --> 00:19:43.410
Check this out!

00:19:43.410 --> 00:19:45.660
Don't look, anyone!

00:19:45.660 --> 00:19:51.000
Are these sexy pictures I see?
And lots of them at that!

00:19:51.000 --> 00:19:53.750
To think they're mixed in with our picture...

00:19:53.750 --> 00:19:56.250
To put it mildly, he's the worst.

00:19:56.250 --> 00:19:59.910
Th-This is, well... Um...

00:19:59.910 --> 00:20:06.580
It's like a sexual harassment time capsule,
but let's put that aside.

00:20:06.580 --> 00:20:10.950
Let's do our best for the old man
watching over us from above!

00:20:10.950 --> 00:20:15.950
I-I just wanna put this out there,
but my dad isn't dead yet.

00:20:22.410 --> 00:20:26.250
Anyway... Seeing how we obtained his legacy...

00:20:28.370 --> 00:20:34.790
I'd like to begin the search for my dad
while also growing the company.

00:20:34.790 --> 00:20:38.160
But what does that mean we're planning to do?

00:20:38.160 --> 00:20:43.000
If the old man went in the Big Gate,
why don't we just go, too?

00:20:43.000 --> 00:20:46.700
It's not nearly that simple, Sis.

00:20:46.700 --> 00:20:52.830
The Big Gate is overseen by a
powerful organization of 12 people.

00:20:52.830 --> 00:20:57.540
Right now, it's locked down and
normal people can't go near it.

00:20:57.540 --> 00:21:00.120
Then, what should we do?

00:21:00.120 --> 00:21:05.500
This is just a suggestion, but what
about if we asked the goddess?

00:21:05.500 --> 00:21:09.200
Oh! That actually might work!

00:21:09.200 --> 00:21:10.540
Goddess?

00:21:10.540 --> 00:21:17.120
The goddess grants you any wish if you
gather enough kirakuri to call her.

00:21:17.120 --> 00:21:21.580
But don't you need an enormous
amount to summon her?

00:21:21.580 --> 00:21:24.410
If I had to roughly estimate...

00:21:24.410 --> 00:21:25.700
"5 x Inheritance Tax"

00:21:25.700 --> 00:21:28.540
"5 x Inheritance Tax"
It's five times the inheritance tax!

00:21:28.540 --> 00:21:30.250
That much money?!

00:21:33.700 --> 00:21:36.540
Let's give it our best shot, President.

00:21:36.540 --> 00:21:38.750
We're family after all.

00:21:38.750 --> 00:21:40.370
Akari...

00:21:40.370 --> 00:21:43.620
That's right. We're here for you, President.

00:21:43.620 --> 00:21:46.160
Have a bit of faith in us!

00:21:46.160 --> 00:21:49.790
Because we're all in this together!

00:21:49.790 --> 00:21:54.290
I think we've found a new
business goal, President!

00:21:57.910 --> 00:21:59.330
Guys...

00:22:00.410 --> 00:22:01.910
Thank you!

00:22:04.750 --> 00:22:07.660
Then, is everyone ready?

00:22:09.700 --> 00:22:14.790
Cheer with me! Kibou, fight!

00:22:14.790 --> 00:22:16.250
Yeah!

00:22:38.790 --> 00:22:43.200
<i>Looking way up into the night sky</i>

00:22:43.200 --> 00:22:47.830
<i>A pretty jewel caught my eye</i>

00:22:47.830 --> 00:22:52.160
<i>Clear skies tomorrow sure would be nice</i>

00:22:52.160 --> 00:22:56.290
<i>Now, make a wish upon a star</i>

00:22:56.290 --> 00:22:58.370
<i>Lazily</i>

00:22:58.370 --> 00:23:01.200
<i>Today comes to a close</i>

00:23:01.200 --> 00:23:05.580
<i>Dead tired and worn out</i>

00:23:05.580 --> 00:23:12.080
<i>Good work</i>
<i>Let's do our best again tomorrow</i>

00:23:12.080 --> 00:23:14.660
<i>Goodnight</i>

00:23:14.660 --> 00:23:16.830
<i>Every day is sparkling</i>

00:23:16.830 --> 00:23:21.370
<i>Just like a box of jewels (sparkling)</i>

00:23:21.370 --> 00:23:23.580
<i>And so brilliant</i>

00:23:23.580 --> 00:23:25.790
<i>Any work undone</i>

00:23:25.790 --> 00:23:30.370
<i>We'll leave for dreamland (sleep tight)</i>

00:23:30.370 --> 00:23:33.870
<i>Let's embark on adventure</i>

00:23:33.870 --> 00:23:38.160
<i>So sleep soundly tonight</i>

00:23:38.160 --> 00:23:43.410
<i>And meet up with me in our dreams</i>

00:23:43.410 --> 00:23:47.000
<i>Sleep tight</i>
